      "writtenOn": "2026-07-31T15:31:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think returning the shadow costs the driver its attribute negotiation. The write handler stores the host\u0027s value and hardware is only written later in enable_lpi, so a write followed by a read-back always returns what was written. its_cpu_init_lpis uses that read-back to see whether the redistributor honoured the Shareability it asked for, and sets RDIST_FLAGS_PROPBASE_NEEDS_FLUSHING when it did not. With the shadow the flag can never be set, so on a redistributor with a fixed Shareability the driver keeps writing property bytes with only a dsb(ishst).\n\nThe ITS half does keep it working: cbaser_read returns hardware and cbaser_write recomputes needs_flush from it. Could it report the hardware\u0027s attribute bits while keeping the address and IDbits from the shadow?",
      "revId": "7833f4481e4f2c8bdfa2bbefbc2a669318744b56",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
